<title>USA: City of Morristown, Tenn., $5.8 mln GOs defeated.</title>
<headline>City of Morristown, Tenn., $5.8 mln GOs defeated.</headline>
<dateline>MORRISTOWN, Tenn 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voters defeated a $5.8 million general obligation bond issue that would have been used for an industrial park, a Morristown city official said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The east Tennessee community voted 3,518 against the proposal and 3,199 for it, city administrator Michael Lutche said of the unofficial tally.</p>
<p>Morristown is about 40 miles northeast of Knoxville and has about 25,000 residents, Lutche said.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
